n we're living with today  gail it's a great question we want to  make sure that we get the people  initially vaccinated we want to make  sure they do that because you don't want  to have people be thinking well the  vaccines are not effective right now  fully vaccinated is two doses of the  mrna and one dose of the j what we're  seeing  and we will move on these data gail when  we get it it looks like boosting  individuals  dramatically increases the level of  protection and that's the reason why  you've heard me over and over again yeah  be very bullish about telling people if  you've been vaccinated six months ago or  more  and you have the mrna get a booster and  if you have the j and j two months or  more ago get boosted whether or not  that's going to ultimately be the  optimal it is entirely conceivable that  that's the case  rather than worry about that now and  confuse people  just get boosted if you're vaccinated we  don't want to confuse people about what  is or is not fully vaccinated get  personal  dr falci as we have these conversations  about covet and we keep talking about  boosters and vaccinations um which i am  an advocate for i have a question though  what happened to the conversation that  hurt immunity can help us get back to  normal  yeah well first of all herd immunity is  a concept that when you have a certain  percentage of people and we don't even  know what that number is nate so we got  to be careful of people who are  vaccinated and fully protected and those  who've been infected and then have a  durable immunity that you will get a  situation where the virus has no place  to go but we have a lot of moving parts  here a  we have 60 million people who are  eligible to be vaccinated among adults  who are not being vaccinated you have  waning immunity it's a reality we just  have to face it when you get vaccinated  you get a high degree of protection but  after several months the immunity wanes  even if you are infected and recover  the im